</td><td align="center"><inline-formula><mml:math xmlns:mml="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" id="M47" name="1471-2474-8-13-i4" overflow="scroll">                              <mml:semantics definitionURL="" encoding="">                                 <mml:mrow>                                    <mml:msubsup>                                       <mml:mi>&#x003c3;</mml:mi>                                       <mml:mi>e</mml:mi>                                       <mml:mn>2</mml:mn>                                    </mml:msubsup>                                 </mml:mrow>                                 <mml:annotation encoding="MathType-MTEF"> MathType@MTEF@5@5@+=feaafiart1ev1aaatCvAUfKttLearuWrP9MDH5MBPbIqV92AaeXatLxBI9gBaebbnrfifHhDYfgasaacH8akY=wiFfYdH8Gipec8Eeeu0xXdbba9frFj0=OqFfea0dXdd9vqai=hGuQ8kuc9pgc9s8qqaq=dirpe0xb9q8qiLsFr0=vr0=vr0dc8meaabaqaciaacaGaaeqabaqabeGadaaakeaaiiGacqWFdpWCdaqhaaWcbaGaemyzaugabaGaeGOmaidaaaaa@30E8@</mml:annotation>                              </mml:semantics>                           </mml:math></inline-formula></td><td align="center">907 &#x000b1; 131</td><td align="center">&#x0003c;0.0001</td></tr></tbody></table><table-wrap-foot><p>sICTP, serum C-terminal telopeptide of type I collagen; sPINP, serum N-terminal propeptide of type I collagen; BMD bone mineral density.</p><p><bold>Note of interpretation</bold>: Results in part (a) suggest that the BMD measurement (mg/cm<sup>2</sup>) for a subject at time <italic>t </italic>(denoted by BMD<sub><italic>t</italic></sub>) can be represented by the equation: BMD<sub><italic>t </italic></sub>= 943 &#x02013; 3.5*Year &#x02013; 9.2* sPINP0, where "Year" is 0, 1, 2, ..., and sPINP0 is the measurement of sPINP at baseline for the subject. In other words, femoral neck BMD was decreased by -3.5 mg/cm<sup>2 </sup>per year. There was no significant association between baseline sPINP and change in BMD (p = 0.4953). The interpretation of variance components is similar to that in Table 3.</p></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap></sec></back></article>